WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.610 --> 00:00:04.980
February may be the shortest month of the
year, but that doesn't mean Netflix is skimping

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:06.940
on the new and original programming.

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:11.920
There's a lot to look forward to in February,
from the Netflix original series Altered Carbon

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:15.540
to Duncan Jones' long-awaited sci-fi noir
Mute.

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:17.570
And that's just scratching the surface.

00:00:17.570 --> 00:00:23.390
Here's everything coming to Netflix in February
2018, starting with the Netflix originals.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:25.720
Altered Carbon: Season 1

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:30.390
Richard K. Morgan's series of hard-boiled
futuristic noir novels has a huge following

00:00:30.390 --> 00:00:34.870
among science fiction fans, and by the looks
of the teasers Netflix has been releasing,

00:00:34.870 --> 00:00:38.190
those fans will have plenty to love about
the upcoming series.

00:00:38.190 --> 00:00:42.760
The story follows Takeshi Kovaks, a soldier
whose mind was imprisoned for hundreds of

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:43.760
years.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:46.870
"How long have I been down?"

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.050
"250 years."

00:00:48.050 --> 00:00:52.350
In the future, he's awoken and given a new
body to solve a murder, kicking off a series

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:55.560
of events that leads him deep into a web of
conspiracy.

00:00:55.560 --> 00:00:59.600
Altered Carbon is definitely going to be one
of the highlights next month, so check it

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:02.190
out on February 2nd.

00:01:02.190 --> 00:01:03.840
On Body and Soul

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:07.900
This Hungarian fantasy drama was announced
as one of the contenders for Best Foreign

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:12.960
Language Film at the 2018 Oscars, but Netflix
isn't waiting to see the results before giving

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.850
it an exclusive international release on their
service.

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:20.040
The story centers on two strangers who find
out that they've been having eerily similar

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.619
dreams every night, so they set out to recreate
those dreams in real life in the hopes of

00:01:24.619 --> 00:01:26.409
figuring out what it all means.

00:01:26.409 --> 00:01:31.560
The Guardian gave On Body and Soul a glowing
review, calling it a "bizarre and brutal tale

00:01:31.560 --> 00:01:33.530
of lovers in the slaughterhouse."

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:37.450
This is definitely one to put on the radar
for February 2nd.

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:39.470
Coach Snoop: Season 1

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:44.030
Starring everyone's favorite D-oh-double-G,
Coach Snoop takes the rapper out of the studio

00:01:44.030 --> 00:01:47.780
and onto the forty-yard-line as the coach
of a youth-league football team.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:51.750
It sounds like the setup for a sports-themed
spinoff of Half Baked, but from the looks

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:56.520
of it, Coach Snoop is taking a long, hard
hit of inspirational drama, focusing on the

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:00.890
real-life stories of at-risk kids fighting
for a future on the gridiron.

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:04.350
There's no comedy here, just a Hail Mary aimed
straight at your heart.

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:06.490
"Y'all ever heard that story of David and
Goliath?

00:02:06.490 --> 00:02:08.700
We are David today, y'all understand?"

00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:09.700
"Yes coach."

00:02:09.700 --> 00:02:13.720
The eight-episode first season kicks off on
February 2.

00:02:13.720 --> 00:02:15.760
Queer Eye: Season 1

00:02:15.760 --> 00:02:20.310
The reboot of the groundbreaking reality show
Queer Eye for the Straight Guy sees five gay

00:02:20.310 --> 00:02:25.560
fashion gurus--the Fab Five, as Netflix describes
them—working with fashion-challenged people

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:28.600
to introduce a little sophistication into
their lives.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:32.010
"I'd like the Fab Five to help me get out
of my comfort zone."

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:36.150
It's the old show rebooted for the world of
today, with a renewed focus on acceptance

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:42.040
for the LGBTQ community—along with plenty
of handmade guacamole and fabulous beards,

00:02:42.040 --> 00:02:43.040
of course.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:46.099
"Ohh, yes balance, yes symmetry."

00:02:46.099 --> 00:02:51.239
Check out Queer Eye when it splashes onto
Netflix on February 7th.

00:02:51.239 --> 00:02:52.739
The Ritual

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:57.520
It wouldn't be a good month on Netflix without
a few original horror releases, and The Ritual

00:02:57.520 --> 00:02:59.129
fills that quota early.

00:02:59.129 --> 00:03:03.069
The story follows four friends on a backpacking
trip through Scandinavia.

00:03:03.069 --> 00:03:07.769
They decide to take a shortcut through a dense
forest—which, of course, is the wrong decision.

00:03:07.769 --> 00:03:11.000
"Go southwest, through here, we cut the journey
in half."

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:12.630
"What, through the forest?"

00:03:12.630 --> 00:03:17.209
The path leads them into a confrontation with
an evil force connected to an ancient Norse

00:03:17.209 --> 00:03:18.209
ritual.

00:03:18.209 --> 00:03:22.430
The movie starts with a fairly standard premise,
but elevates it with beautiful scenery and

00:03:22.430 --> 00:03:27.350
a refreshing self awareness that takes this
a notch above your typical paranormal horror

00:03:27.350 --> 00:03:28.350
film.

00:03:28.350 --> 00:03:30.080
"Well, this is clearly the house we get murdered
in."

00:03:30.080 --> 00:03:32.950
Enter the woods on February 9th.

00:03:32.950 --> 00:03:33.950
The Trader

00:03:33.950 --> 00:03:39.420
This Netflix original documentary offers a
bleak look into rural life in Eastern Europe,

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:43.940
centering on a man traveling across Georgia
selling knickknacks and second-hand clothes

00:03:43.940 --> 00:03:48.480
in exchange for the only currency with any
meaning in a land stricken by poverty and

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:49.940
hunger: potatoes.

00:03:49.940 --> 00:03:52.940
The Trader is sure to be an eye-opening experience.

00:03:52.940 --> 00:03:56.470
Step outside your comfort zone and queue it
up on February 9.

00:03:56.470 --> 00:03:59.099
Fate/Apocrypha: Part 2

00:03:59.099 --> 00:04:04.610
The first part of Netflix's original anime
series Fate/Apocrypha was released in 2017

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:10.099
to generally favorable reviews, and the second
part of Season 1 is slated to roll out February

00:04:10.099 --> 00:04:12.930
9, completing the first season story arc.

00:04:12.930 --> 00:04:15.659
Tune in for part two this winter.

00:04:15.659 --> 00:04:19.569
My Next Guest Needs No Introduction With David
Letterman: George Clooney

00:04:19.569 --> 00:04:24.659
Late night icon David Letterman teamed up
with Netflix in January 2018 for the first

00:04:24.659 --> 00:04:29.330
installment of his new interview series, which
saw Letterman sitting down with former president

00:04:29.330 --> 00:04:33.559
Barack Obama for an hour-long interview about
politics and beards.

00:04:33.559 --> 00:04:37.020
"You and I are the same age."

00:04:37.020 --> 00:04:40.360
"He's got this biblical beard."

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.699
"Do you have a staff?"

00:04:43.699 --> 00:04:48.370
Unlike most of its shows, Netflix is releasing
this series one episode at a time, and the

00:04:48.370 --> 00:04:50.960
next one will feature George Clooney in the
guest's seat.

00:04:50.960 --> 00:04:53.309
Take a look on February 9th.

00:04:53.309 --> 00:04:55.569
Seeing Allred

00:04:55.569 --> 00:05:00.369
Netflix is chiming in on the wave of allegations
that permeated the news in 2017 with Seeing

00:05:00.369 --> 00:05:04.550
Allred, a documentary following activist attorney
Gloria Allred.

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:09.770
As a lawyer, Allred has represented multiple
clients involved in lawsuits against famous

00:05:09.770 --> 00:05:13.250
celebrities, and is a vocal opponent of discrimination.

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:16.219
See the documentary on February 9th.

00:05:16.219 --> 00:05:17.789
When We First Met

00:05:17.789 --> 00:05:22.499
Starring Adam Devine from Workaholics, When
We First Met is a comedy fantasy about a guy

00:05:22.499 --> 00:05:26.009
who found the girl of his dreams… and then
blew his chance with her.

00:05:26.009 --> 00:05:29.629
Three years later, he gets the chance to go
back in time to the night he messed everything

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:31.529
up to try and fix things.

00:05:31.529 --> 00:05:33.789
Queue it up on February 9.

00:05:33.789 --> 00:05:36.189
Greenhouse Academy: Season 2

00:05:36.189 --> 00:05:41.440
This high school series debuted its first
season in 2017 and follows two twin teenagers

00:05:41.440 --> 00:05:44.080
who enroll at a futuristic boarding school.

00:05:44.080 --> 00:05:47.990
Unfortunately, there's some kind of global
conspiracy in the works, and it's up to them

00:05:47.990 --> 00:05:51.300
to stop it before the evil masterminds can
destroy the earth.

00:05:51.300 --> 00:05:54.029
Also, there's a bunch of teen drama and whatnot.

00:05:54.029 --> 00:05:55.740
"What is this the fourth grade, or something?"

00:05:59.569 --> 00:06:04.040
If you're over the age of, say, 14, there
probably isn't a whole lot here for you, but

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:07.749
if you're a 12-year-old girl, you might just
find your new favorite show.

00:06:07.749 --> 00:06:10.550
Season 2 lands on February 14.

00:06:10.550 --> 00:06:11.610
Love Per Square Foot

00:06:11.610 --> 00:06:17.099
Touted as the first mainstream Indian film
to be released by Netflix on a global scale,

00:06:17.099 --> 00:06:21.210
Love Per Square Foot is a romantic comedy
about a man and a woman who decide to get

00:06:21.210 --> 00:06:24.550
married so that they can afford an apartment
in Mumbai.

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:27.849
It's bound to be an interesting experience,
if nothing else.

00:06:27.849 --> 00:06:30.159
Check it out on February 14.

00:06:30.159 --> 00:06:32.530
Re:Mind: Season 1

00:06:32.530 --> 00:06:36.960
This Japanese series starts with 11 classmates
who wake up in a locked room with no idea

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:38.089
how they got there.

00:06:38.089 --> 00:06:42.369
The more clues they uncover about their situation,
the deeper the threat to their lives appears

00:06:42.369 --> 00:06:43.369
to be.

00:06:43.369 --> 00:06:47.460
Figure out the mystery when Re:Mind lands
on February 15.

00:06:47.460 --> 00:06:49.520
First Team: Juventus

00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:54.500
This documentary mini-series tags along with
the stars of the Italian football team Juventus

00:06:54.500 --> 00:06:59.740
as they kick their way through the grueling
2017-2018 season.

00:06:59.740 --> 00:07:03.810
First Team promises to go behind the scenes
with the team to reveal their lives both on

00:07:03.810 --> 00:07:05.189
and off the field.

00:07:05.189 --> 00:07:10.490
If you're a fan of the black and white, check
out the first three episodes on February 16.

00:07:10.490 --> 00:07:12.099
Everything Sucks!: Season 1

00:07:12.099 --> 00:07:16.099
Move over, '80s nostalgia—there's a new
decade in town.

00:07:16.099 --> 00:07:22.250
Everything Sucks follows a high school A/V
club in 1996, when VCRs, Discmans, and iron-on

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.020
backpack patches reigned supreme."

00:07:24.020 --> 00:07:27.770
If you miss the days when Alanis Morissette
and the Goo Goo Dolls were the soundtrack

00:07:27.770 --> 00:07:32.330
for everything, check out the first season
of Everything Sucks! on February 16.

00:07:32.330 --> 00:07:36.490
You might regret it, but that would just mean
the show really nailed what the '90s were

00:07:36.490 --> 00:07:37.619
all about.

00:07:37.619 --> 00:07:39.800
The Joel McHale Show with Joel McHale

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:45.559
You may recognize Joel McHale from the long-running
NBC show Community or from his E! series The

00:07:45.559 --> 00:07:50.169
Soup—or any of the long list of movies and
shows where he's inevitably played a horrible,

00:07:50.169 --> 00:07:51.479
morally bankrupt person.

00:07:51.479 --> 00:07:56.800
"I can pick up this pencil, tell you its name
is Steve and go like this --- and part of

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:00.020
you dies, just a little bit on the inside."

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:04.989
On February 18th, McHale lands on Netflix
with The Joel McHale Show with Joel McHale,

00:08:04.989 --> 00:08:09.599
a ridiculously named show that will see McHale
going back to his sketch talk show roots,

00:08:09.599 --> 00:08:10.840
green screen and all.

00:08:10.840 --> 00:08:13.239
Can we say McHale any more?

00:08:13.239 --> 00:08:15.159
FullMetal Alchemist

00:08:15.159 --> 00:08:19.839
Don't get too excited about a Netflix-produced
version of the classic anime FullMetal Alchemist—this

00:08:19.839 --> 00:08:25.910
is a rebranding of the 2017 live-action adaptation
produced in Japan, a film that wasn't particularly

00:08:25.910 --> 00:08:27.530
well received by critics.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:31.469
If you haven't seen it yet, you can form your
own opinion when the movie premieres on Netflix

00:08:31.469 --> 00:08:33.380
on February 19th.

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:36.300
The Frankenstein Chronicles: Seasons 1 and
2

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:41.099
For residents of the UK, The Frankenstein
Chronicles might already be a familiar show.

00:08:41.099 --> 00:08:45.880
The series stars Sean Bean as a detective
in the 1800s who's on the trail of a madman

00:08:45.880 --> 00:08:48.839
who may or may not be Dr. Frankenstein.

00:08:48.839 --> 00:08:53.550
Netflix picked up the acclaimed horror mystery
series in December 2017 for global release

00:08:53.550 --> 00:08:55.940
and rebranded it as a Netflix original.

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:59.470
Tune in when both seasons hit on February
20th.

00:08:59.470 --> 00:09:01.529
Seven Seconds: Season 1

00:09:01.529 --> 00:09:06.410
After a tragic, racially charged accident
involving a black teenager in New York City,

00:09:06.410 --> 00:09:11.089
one family fights to prevent a bureaucratic
cover-up in this harrowing crime thriller.

00:09:11.089 --> 00:09:14.709
Seven Seconds stars Regina King and Clare-Hope
Ashity.

00:09:14.709 --> 00:09:18.360
Take a look when the first season lands on
February 23.

00:09:18.360 --> 00:09:20.649
Marseille: Season 2

00:09:20.649 --> 00:09:25.079
Netflix's French-language political thriller
Marseille hasn't made a ton of waves yet,

00:09:25.079 --> 00:09:29.839
but fans of the show have been hoping for
a second season ever since the first one debuted

00:09:29.839 --> 00:09:30.900
in 2016.

00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:35.500
The show centers on the mayor of Marseille
as he squares off against his successor and

00:09:35.500 --> 00:09:39.870
rival, and it offers plenty of political intrigue
and bureaucratic backstabbing.

00:09:39.870 --> 00:09:44.240
It's a touch formulaic, but it should satisfy
any political thriller buff on the hunt for

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:46.160
a bingeable House of Cards replacement.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:50.300
Catch the second season on February 23.

00:09:50.300 --> 00:09:51.529
Mute

00:09:51.529 --> 00:09:55.520
Director Duncan Jones has been working on
this film for over a decade, and the wait

00:09:55.520 --> 00:09:58.339
is finally over on February 23rd.

00:09:58.339 --> 00:10:03.050
In a near-future Berlin, a mute bartender
forges a path through the city's twisted underbelly

00:10:03.050 --> 00:10:05.430
on a quest to find his missing girlfriend.

00:10:05.430 --> 00:10:10.779
Alexander Skarsgard stars, with Paul Rudd
and Justin Theroux in supporting roles.

00:10:10.779 --> 00:10:11.870
Ugly Delicious

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:16.459
Get your forks ready, because there's a brand
new food and culture show on the horizon.

00:10:16.459 --> 00:10:20.889
Ugly Delicious dives into on-the-street cuisine
with chef David Chang.

00:10:20.889 --> 00:10:21.889
Rude waiters?

00:10:21.889 --> 00:10:22.890
Dirty bathrooms?

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:26.220
In Ugly Delicious, it doesn't matter as long
as the food is good.

00:10:26.220 --> 00:10:28.870
Take the trip on February 23rd.

00:10:28.870 --> 00:10:30.970
Derren Brown: The Push

00:10:30.970 --> 00:10:35.560
Illusionist Derren Brown is known for his
controversial shows and psychological experiments,

00:10:35.560 --> 00:10:39.740
and Derren Brown: The Push is bound to be
an interesting addition to the performer's

00:10:39.740 --> 00:10:40.740
line-up.

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:44.360
Most of the details regarding the show are
being kept quiet, so we'll all have to wait

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:49.630
until February 27 to find out where Derren
Brown takes us next.

00:10:49.630 --> 00:10:51.410
Original stand-up comedy

00:10:51.410 --> 00:10:55.600
Netflix has been loading up on stand-up specials
in the past couple months, but the streaming

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:59.040
service is only bringing three new specials
into the fold in February.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:01.319
Kavin Jay: Everybody Calm Down!

00:11:01.319 --> 00:11:06.019
Was originally slated for a January release,
but has since been pushed back to February

00:11:06.019 --> 00:11:07.019
2nd.

00:11:07.019 --> 00:11:12.180
On February 6, you can tune in to Fred Armisen:
Standup For Drummers, and February 27th will

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:16.389
see comedian and actor Marlon Wayans' hour-long
stand-up special, Woke-ish.

00:11:16.389 --> 00:11:19.300
That covers all the Netflix originals coming
in February.

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:24.370
Now here are all the other movies and TV shows
arriving next month.

00:11:24.370 --> 00:11:25.610
New Movies

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:29.750
February is going to be a great month to relive
the action classics of the past.

00:11:29.750 --> 00:11:34.000
Quentin Tarantino's Kill Bill Volumes 1 and
2 will both be arriving on the first of the

00:11:34.000 --> 00:11:38.129
month, along with 3000 Miles to Graceland,
to name a few.

00:11:38.129 --> 00:11:42.370
For more dramatic fare, Netflix is doubling
down on their gangland classics with Martin

00:11:42.370 --> 00:11:43.800
Scorsese's Goodfellas.

00:11:43.800 --> 00:11:48.220
That arrives on the first of the month, along
with the Ocean's Eleven trilogy and the 2008

00:11:48.220 --> 00:11:50.480
Oscar-winner The Hurt Locker.

00:11:50.480 --> 00:11:54.879
And if those don't get the Valentine's mood
rolling, Netflix is rolling out every unromantic

00:11:54.879 --> 00:11:56.720
comedy it can get its hand on.

00:11:56.720 --> 00:12:02.279
The first of the month is heralding five American
Pie movies, along with Meet the Parents, and

00:12:02.279 --> 00:12:07.120
it's sequel with the funny name, and John
C. Reilly's irreverent, musical saga Walk

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:08.500
Hard: The Dewey Cox Story.

00:12:08.500 --> 00:12:10.079
"Two things you need to know.

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:13.900
I'm the king, and number two is LOOK OUT MAN!

00:12:13.900 --> 00:12:15.120
Look at that!"

00:12:15.709 --> 00:12:20.800
And speaking of music, February 1st will also
see some great new documentary releases, like

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:22.879
How the Beatles Changed the World.

00:12:22.879 --> 00:12:28.339
Later in the month, look for Winnie, a 2017
documentary about Winnie Mandela, activist

00:12:28.339 --> 00:12:30.410
and former wife of Nelson Mandela.

00:12:30.410 --> 00:12:32.730
That premieres on February 26.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:37.160
Perhaps mercifully, Netflix is only adding
two family films in February.

00:12:37.160 --> 00:12:42.000
Less mercifully, one of them is The Emoji
Movie, one of the most soul-crushingly bad

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.769
animated films in history.

00:12:43.769 --> 00:12:46.110
You can look forward to that on February 8th.

00:12:46.110 --> 00:12:48.740
Ella Enchanted also arrives on the first of
the month.

00:12:48.740 --> 00:12:53.829
After the kids go to bed, turn off the lights
and enjoy Netflix's new thriller lineup.

00:12:53.829 --> 00:12:59.720
Look for Scream 3 on the 1st, the 2016 Cabin
Fever remake on the 2nd, Blood Money on the

00:12:59.720 --> 00:13:02.190
17th, and Dismissed on the 19th.

00:13:02.190 --> 00:13:07.449
Finally, February 24th sees the arrival of
Jeepers Creepers 3.

00:13:07.449 --> 00:13:09.079
New television

00:13:09.079 --> 00:13:13.260
Fans of thrilling television will have a lot
to look forward to come February.

00:13:13.260 --> 00:13:19.040
On the first of the month, Season 4 of Z Nation
arrives, followed by Season 1 of Valor 5 days

00:13:19.040 --> 00:13:23.430
later, and Season 1 of The Imposters the following
day on February 7th.

00:13:23.430 --> 00:13:28.249
After that, keep an eye out for the thrilling
fifth and final season of Bates Motel on the

00:13:28.249 --> 00:13:29.249
20th.

00:13:29.249 --> 00:13:30.519
Thanks for watching!

00:13:30.519 --> 00:13:33.420
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:13:33.420 --> 00:13:35.779
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

